{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"451ae9891f6725f72cbd8f16340ce3314b25a347b5fb167318ee573b46400f37","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP adapter for unlink_tickets","key_entities":["src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets","rebar.unlink","relation","FastMCP schema","docs/mcp-reference.md","scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_unlink_relation.py","restoring-shallow-blobfish"],"problem_keywords":["mcp schema","unlink","relation selector","parameter parity","write surface","interface divergence"],"propositions":["MCP unlink_tickets registered callable signature omits the optional relation parameter supported by the public library contract","MCP unlink_tickets does not forward the relation parameter to rebar.unlink, causing pair-scoped fallback behavior instead of relation-specific removal","The live FastMCP schema does not advertise relation as an optional field, preventing callers from expressing relation-specific edge selection","When a ticket pair holds multiple relations, MCP unlink removes the most-recent edge rather than an explicitly requested relation","The signed parity ruling on restoring-shallow-blobfish requires identical relation-selector support across library, CLI, and MCP write surfaces"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787536051482082001,"uuid":"d31a066b-3cb6-4f38-9716-cc92595a1951"}